## Stage 1 — Elevator System Basics: Entities, States, and Button Types

- Before writing a single line of code it helps to name every moving part in plain English.
- Core entities: States an ElevatorCar can be in: - IDLE — the car is stopped and has no pending stops.
- - MOVING UP — the car is travelling upward and serving stops along the way.
- - MOVING DOWN — the car is travelling downward and serving stops along the way.

*Applies **low-level-design-systems** to the decision above.*

**Observable outcome:** - MOVING DOWN — the car is travelling downward and serving stops along the way.

